string standalone.bf_runnerSchedule()
{
// Backfill engine - schedule wrapper (DRAFT v2, 2026-11-12, Phase 2)
// Picks at most 2 runnable Runs (Status Queued or Paused_Budget, oldest Created_Time first) and calls
// standalone.bf_runnerCore once for each, one after the other (no parallel runs; COQL sub-concurrency).
// The Runner itself refuses locked runs (TC-13), mismatched versions (TC-12) and other statuses.
// Declaration history (measured in this org on 2026-11-12):
//   - v1 was declared as void standalone.bf_runnerSchedule(). Saving it failed with:
//       Invalid return Type void. Category standalone returns string (Line :1)
//   - Together with the earlier Map refusal (Invalid return Type Map. Category standalone returns string),
//     this confirms that a standalone function can only return string (knowledge base 5.2).
//   - v2 is declared as string standalone.bf_runnerSchedule() and returns a one-line run summary, e.g.
//       SCHEDULE done attempted=2 [run <id> -> <first 120 chars of result>] [run <id> -> ...]
//     Zoho may drop underscores from displayed return strings (knowledge base 5.2); the fixed words of the summary avoid them.
//   - The processing itself is unchanged from v1. The info lines are kept as they were.
//   - The real schedule assignment needs the schedule category (void schedule.<name>), which is created
//     separately from the Schedules screen, e.g. void schedule.bf_runnerschedule() with the same body minus
//     the return statements (or a thin body that calls this function). This file stays the standalone
//     version for manual runs and testing.
// COQL on the custom modules Backfill_Runs / Backfill_Logs (measured in this org on 2026-11-12):
//   - COQL works on both custom modules via connection crm_module.
//   - Rows found = HTTP 200 with data. No rows = HTTP 204 with an empty body, which means there is nothing to run.
//   - If the query fails (error code such as INVALID_QUERY / INVALID_MODULE, an exception, or an
//     unexpected body), this wrapper only writes the reason with info and ends normally. It never guesses
//     a Run id and never falls back to Search (Search has an index delay; knowledge base 2.1).
// Result text in the summary is cut to the first 120 characters (subString errors past the end, so the
// length is checked first; knowledge base 6.2).
	api = "https://www.zohoapis.jp/crm/v8";
	q = "select id, Name, Status, Created_Time from Backfill_Runs where Status in ('Queued','Paused_Budget') order by Created_Time asc limit 2";
	qMap = Map();
	qMap.put("select_query",q);
	resp = Map();
	coqlOk = true;
	failReason = "";
	try
	{
		resp = invokeurl
		[
			url :api + "/coql"
			type :POST
			parameters:qMap.toString()
			connection:"crm_module"
		];
	}
	catch (eQ)
	{
		coqlOk = false;
		failReason = "COQL call raised an exception: " + eQ.toString();
	}
	runIds = List();
	if(coqlOk)
	{
		if(resp == null || resp.toString() == "")
		{
			info "bf_runnerSchedule: no runnable run (empty COQL response)";
		}
		else if(resp.get("data") == null)
		{
			if(resp.get("code") != null)
			{
				coqlOk = false;
				failReason = "COQL on Backfill_Runs failed: " + resp.get("code").toString() + " " + ifnull(resp.get("message"),"").toString();
			}
			else
			{
				info "bf_runnerSchedule: no runnable run";
			}
		}
		else
		{
			for each r in resp.get("data")
			{
				if(r.get("id") != null)
				{
					runIds.add(r.get("id").toString());
				}
			}
		}
	}
	summaryParts = "";
	if(coqlOk == false)
	{
		info "bf_runnerSchedule: ended without running anything. " + failReason;
		failHead = failReason;
		if(failHead.length() > 120)
		{
			failHead = failHead.subString(0,120);
		}
		summaryParts = " [not run: " + failHead + "]";
	}
	for each rid in runIds
	{
		resultHead = "";
		try
		{
			result = standalone.bf_runnerCore(rid);
			info "bf_runnerSchedule: run " + rid + " -> " + result;
			resultHead = ifnull(result,"").toString();
		}
		catch (eR)
		{
			info "bf_runnerSchedule: run " + rid + " raised an exception: " + eR.toString();
			resultHead = "EXCEPTION " + eR.toString();
		}
		if(resultHead.length() > 120)
		{
			resultHead = resultHead.subString(0,120);
		}
		summaryParts = summaryParts + " [run " + rid + " -> " + resultHead + "]";
	}
	attempted = runIds.size().toString();
	info "bf_runnerSchedule: done, runs attempted=" + attempted;
	summary = "SCHEDULE done attempted=" + attempted + summaryParts;
	return summary;
}
